WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.269
Today, we're gonna talk about the

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.009
ontology, what it is, why it

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.909
matters, how you actually use it to

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.629
build decision-centric systems in

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.929
the real world.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.729
So if we think about what is an

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.489
ontology? It's the nouns and verbs

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.829
that make up your business, right?

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.449
So in this manufacturing example, I

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.509
have plants and warehouses that

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.169
I'm supplying plants from

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.989
warehouses, right, I'm shipping

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.689
product to customers.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.909
So this really reflects

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.349
the grown truth about how your

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.869
business is actually operating.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.689
There's complex interconnected

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:29.709
relationships, right.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.629
So. As we model this

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.229
into the ontology, the goal is to

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:35.169
actually model how your business

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.969
is actually operating, not how these

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.449
other systems need it so they can

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.269
work.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.189
So, if we think about that in

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.809
a decision-centric system, what do I

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.809
need to be able to make decisions,

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.069
right? I need three things, I need

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.809
the data, I need logic,

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.529
and I need actions, right, so I need

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:51.869
data, the logic, the actions.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.649
The data represents what the current

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.749
state of my business is, the logic

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.209
about how do I think about those

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.729
things, and the actions I can take

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.579
to affect the real world.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.239
Right, so if we can dig into that a

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.899
little bit further here on the data

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.299
sources, right, I'm connecting to

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.899
all my different enterprise systems,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.259
whether they're homegrown, out of

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.319
the box software, legacy, new

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.979
stuff in the web, doesn't matter.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.819
We have 300 out of box connectors

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.399
that you can actually connect to

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.399
stuff, or with MMDP, you

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.079
can connect to things like Snowflake

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.839
and Databricks and BigQuery and

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.019
virtualized data that's already

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.619
sitting in those enterprise data

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.579
lakes and pull it in and just use

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.419
that as part of your ontology,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.819
right? So this really is about

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.399
making it seamless connecting.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.839
To that data across your business.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.399
Then sources of logic, right?

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.239
So these could be really simple.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.439
That could be an Excel spreadsheet,

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:38.339
rules-based logic.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.339
It could be ML models, forecast,

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.039
third-party optimizers you bought.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.279
They can be living inside of the

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.599
platform, outside of the the

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:45.799
platform. We integrate with all

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:46.859
these different tools no matter

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.719
where the model or sources of

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.559
the logic are.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.079
We wanna integrate that and actually

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.779
model that into the semantic object

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.599
about how, for example,

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.539
a warehouse works.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.939
What's the logic associated about

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.119
how to think about that warehouse?

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.959
Then the last is

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.779
Systems of action right so if

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:04.339
I think get the data I get the logic

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.619
to how to think about it now What

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.379
actions can I take and how do I make

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.279
it real? So whether it's SAP and

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.159
I want to write back to SAP to

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.959
create an STO to move product from A

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.959
to B across my Network right those

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.699
should be modeled in here as the

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.359
actions I can take there can be

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.579
other things that are on the plant

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.739
Floor they can be Financial

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.759
systems you name it will connect

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.479
into those whether they're legacy or

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.939
the on-prem. They're at the edge

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:27.919
They're in the cloud. They can be

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.989
web hooks you name it, we connect

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:31.609
with those things to really drive

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.609
back those actions into

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:34.629
the enterprise.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.669
So if we bring all the data,

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.909
the logic, the action together here,

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:40.769
then I have this ontology that

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.969
is very rich, showing me

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.849
my actual digital twin of how my

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.609
business is operating, how to think

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:47.649
about it with the logic and what

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.049
actions I'm gonna take to affect

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.669
that system.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.609
So then on top of that,

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:53.849
and we can then build these

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.529
workflows and analytics and looks

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.209
really are a by-product of the

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.369
workflows that I'm building.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.829
So a workflow across many different

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.489
business processes or business

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.349
systems that I connect together with

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.329
the people, the process, and

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.469
I really then start to bubble up

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:08.909
the insights there.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.469
And then we start to add other

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.129
things in here like automations,

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.229
right? So now can we have generative

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.289
AI models integrated through AIP

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.239
and AIP logic, for example.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.339
That now are helping actually go

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.859
reason about it because they have

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.959
access to the ontology, the LLM now

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.779
has access to context,

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.719
not just the data, the context about

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:28.779
how my business operates.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.619
So the LM can have access to

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.799
the logic about how to think about

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.359
it. So the LM can call a

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:34.659
deterministic model.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.699
It can then drive an action

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:37.839
to write back.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.559
So instead of people having to

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.499
swivel chair from a dashboard

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.999
over to another tool to figure out

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.499
how to make it real, we'll

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.749
orchestrate those complex

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.329
Actions on the back end to make it

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.369
real and that's where really where

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.969
automations come in bringing

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.889
reasoning into this process

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.749
and ontology really is that

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.309
Context of how your business is

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.069
operating because the LMS were not

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.969
trained on your business's data or

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:00.970
processes

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.079
is the products in SDK.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.919
So this is where we can build data

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.899
products, rich applications, whether

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.819
that's in a mobile app for the

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.899
plant floor, it's a custom

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.319
React app to interact with my

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.139
customers, or it could be through

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.939
the ontology SDK, where I actually

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.999
create a custom SDK of

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.139
my ontology.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:22.379
So an SDK of business

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.679
and business process that I can

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.159
build different applications, back

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.219
integrations, I can integrate that

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.459
SDK that has agented workflows.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.019
Into my existing applications.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.299
Lots of different and really great

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.859
stuff that you can do by powering

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.719
different SDKs throughout

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:36.499
your business.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.079
This really opens up the way that

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.339
you integrate it and really improves

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.179
the usability, which improves speed

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.659
and time to value.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:44.979
So all of this comes together with

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:46.979
the goal of AI and humans

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.659
working together on the ontology.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.119
And the goal over time is to

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.659
automate more and more of your

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.239
business, so really what you need is

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.039
the ontolgy to model the data, the

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.379
logic, the actions to drive

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.999
decisions in your business

